From workstream 05, for workstream 04 to integrate (shared core).

- ledger/gateway: besides the general token (unchanged), the owner can
  issue a token per sender (ai | mcp): rotate-capability with
  params.source replaces that sender's token only, revoke-capability
  removes it. A sender's token is accepted for requests of that source
  only; whoami says which token it is; the view lists sender token
  versions, never hashes. Records from before have no capabilities and
  work as before.
- With workstream 03's consent naming source mcp (its patch), 03 and 05
  no longer turn each other's token into BadCapability.
- 0002b's rebuild on a Duplicate is not used for SendCaravan (it
  carries the Citizen's caravan seq), as AUTH-ROUTES §4 asks.

Test agent-wallet-sender-capability (no key made or used, nothing
signed: plain records, manual mode stops every request at the gate):
4 pass; agent-wallet-run-facts 3 pass.
